  <rdf:Description rdf:nodeID="commodity_stave_cbd16e98a962c48561422fe10c4300cd906a8a1ab1421a54af6de5a751cf0a2e1a">
    <crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>(stave, -s, stave, -z) stave | stick; cane; club or clublike weapon; staff (MED s.v. staf n.) | clearly some sort of packing unit for copper pans, but meaning unknown | clearly some sort of packing unit (measure?) of kettles, but exact meaning unknown | stave for making crossbows | probably the bow of a cross-bow | staves for a bill, which is an obsolete military weapon used chiefly by infantry; varying in form from a simple concave blade with a long wooden handle, to a kind of concave axe with a spike at the back and its shaft terminating in a spear-head; a halberd (OED s.v. bill n.1 2) | stave for spears</crm:P190_has_symbolic_content>
    <crm:P2_has_type rdf:resource="http://vocab.getty.edu/aat/300435416"/>
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.cidoc-crm.org/cidoc-crm/E33_Linguistic_Object"/>
  </rdf:Description>
